{"name":"Frankly Earnest","hex":"#e2dbca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frankly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In a frank or candid manner, especially in a way that may seem too open, excessively honest, or slightly blunt.","In truth, to tell the truth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frankly"},{"term":"earnest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Gravity; serious purpose; earnestness.","Seriousness; reality; actuality (as opposed to joking or pretence)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be serious with; use in earnest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/earnest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frankly","blocks":[{"text":"Frankly is a memoir by former Scottish First Minister Nicola Sturgeon, published by Pan Macmillan. Although its official release date was set for 14 August 2025, the book was made available early on 11 August 2025 at some Waterstones branches. The subtitle of the memoir is \"The Revelatory Memoir from Scotland's First Female and Longest-Serving First Minister\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/FranklyNicolaSturgeon.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankly","wikidata":"Q135902968"},{"title":"Earnest","blocks":[{"text":"Earnest is a masculine given name and a surname which may refer to:"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earnest","wikidata":"Q5326924"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"frankly":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/43/En-us-frankly.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/43/En-us-frankly.ogg/En-us-frankly.ogg.mp3"}],"earnest":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/En-us-earnest.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.or